[d44d — the slab smeared theorem, exact kappa(m), the interacting cross-check]
  banner: exact truncated-series arithmetic (the d43a machinery, ported
  verbatim); mp.dps = 50; threshold 1e-30; SG0 at ORD = 12 / L = 12 (the
  d43a code path, re-anchored); KG1/KG2/KG3 at ORD = 4 (EXACT truncation:
  a Delta^p coefficient of series products/inverses depends only on input
  orders <= p; gated below at 1e-40 entrywise and on the kappa anchors).
  Exit 1 ONLY on anchor/extraction breakage; KG1 w-dependence, KG2 non-fit,
  and every KG3 verdict are pre-registered DELIVERED outcomes at exit 0.
  Round-1 minor-2, stated as designed: clean-cell collapse CONSTANTS and
  all verdict lines are DELIVERED-VERDICT content, not exit gates — their
  integrity rides on byte-identical determinism of this .out (SG5); the
  exit-gated layer is anchors/extraction/recognition/collapse-form only.
  Deterministic: no RNG, no wall clock; rerun byte-identical (SG5).

  PINNED TEST-WEIGHT FAMILY (KG1; declared BEFORE any verdict):
  log-uniform site weights over the slab: for width w, phi_j =
  (1/(j+1)) / H_w at site base+j, j = 0..w-1, H_w = sum_{k=1..w} 1/k.
  Exact values: w=1: (1); w=2: (2/3, 1/3); w=3: (6/11, 3/11, 2/11);
  w=4: (12/25, 6/25, 4/25, 3/25).
  The weights enter as the v2 p1 SS7 log-smeared slab observable read at
  leading coefficient order (log J_n = Delta^p A_n + h.o., so the SS7
  log-smear IS the phi-weighted singleton-coefficient sum at this order):
    COMPOSITE arm:  Abar_w(b) = sum_{j<w} phi_j A^rule_{{b+j}}.
  The pin's literal 'regions R = contiguous blocks' reading is run as the
    BLOCK arm:      A^rule_{R_w(b)},  R_w(b) = {b..b+w-1},
                    C_R = sum_{n in R} m beta_n + sum_{bonds meeting R} k.
  Identification (both arms): the d43a tau first-moment construction on
  the pair at bases (0, r): tau(delta,s,s') = sum_{r=1..rmax} r *
  sum_i [A(0), A(r)]_{(i,s),(i+delta,s')}; D(s,s') = sum_delta delta*tau;
  rmax = w+1 (EXC) / w+3 (LT) = the exact kernel-support bound; the
  rmax+1 completeness slot is gated ZERO on every wrap-clean cell.
  Declared: by translation covariance the phi-weighted mean pair
  separation equals the base separation r exactly, so on wrap-clean
  lattices the composite-arm collapse constant is weight-family
  independent (the cancellation-order content of the conversion note);
  the log-uniform family is the pinned instance run here.

  WRAP CENSUS (support lemma, declared BEFORE verdicts): the LT defect
  kernel of either arm spans sites [b-2, b+w+1]; the pair at separation r
  is seam-free iff r <= w+3 (front bound) and r < L-(w+3) (back bound).
  At L=12 these overlap for w in {3,4}: the LT cells (L=12, w=3|4,
  COMPOSITE|BLOCK) are WRAP-CONTAMINATED — excluded from the theorem
  gate, delivered with flag WRAP, with the L=16 twins carrying the clean
  statement. All EXC cells (kernel [b-1, b+w], rmax = w+1) and all L=16
  cells are seam-free.

  SG4 FLOAT ENTRY POINTS (enumerated): (1) all series arithmetic is
  mpmath binary at dps 50 (rational inputs with non-power-of-2
  denominators are 1e-50-rounded on entry; hence gates at 1e-30, never
  equality on mpf); (2) kappa/constant recognition: exact binary value ->
  Fraction via continued-fraction best approximation, denominator cap
  1e15, gated |x - p/q| < 1e-30 (max residual and max denominator
  reported in SG4); downstream ansatz solve/verify runs in EXACT Fraction
  arithmetic with ZERO tolerance on the recognized rationals; (3) the KG3
  fixture constants (7/10, 1/2, 9/10, -2/5, 11/10, 1/5) enter as dps-50
  mpf. No other float entry points exist.

